# PRD — {{feature_or_product_name}}

> **What this document is.** A product decision record: the problem, the people it
> affects, and how the experience changes. It is the input to design and
> engineering — not a design or engineering document.
>
> **What it is NOT.** No architecture, no data model, no API shapes, no migration
> plan, no file paths, no acceptance criteria. Those belong to `ARCHITECTURE.md`,
> `DESIGN.md` and the per-change execution spec. If you are writing them here,
> stop: you are in the wrong document.
>
> **Tag every claim with its provenance:** `[data]` (measured), `[research]`
> (user interview / usability session), `[hunch]` (belief, not yet validated).
> Write `[needs input]` instead of inventing a number. A guessed metric presented
> as a fact is worse than an honest gap.

